---
title: Jerk Meatballs in Coconut Curry Sauce
description: Big time Caribbean flavors with tender and juicy pork meatballs swimming in a creamy coconut curry sauce.
servings: 4
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 40 minutes
total time: 50 minutes
category: Main Entree
course: Main
cuisine: Caribbean
author: Quin Liburd
source: https://www.butterbeready.com/jerk-meatballs-in-coconut-curry-sauce/
tags: [caribbean, meatballs, pork, curry, coconut, weeknight, one-pan]
---

In a #large bowl{}, combine @ground pork{1.5%lbs}, @large egg{1}, @seasoned panko breadcrumbs{1/2%cup}, @garlic{4%cloves, finely minced}, @sliced scallions{1/4%cup, plus more for garnish}, @jerk seasoning{2%tablespoons}, @ginger paste{1%tsp} or @freshly grated ginger{2%tsp}, and @kosher salt and freshly ground black pepper{to taste}.

Use your hands to bring the meatball mixture together until just combined — careful not to overwork the meat.

Use a #spring-loaded scooper{} to form about 20-22 meatballs. Roll in the palm of your hands until smooth. Place onto a #baking sheet{} or large plate.

In a #large non-stick skillet{} over medium heat, warm @unsalted butter{2%tablespoons} and @olive oil{1%tablespoon}. Once sizzling, add the meatballs. Work in batches — careful not to overcrowd.

Fry the meatballs until browned and lightly crisp, ~{3%minutes} on each side. Place the seared meatballs onto a cleaned #baking sheet{} and repeat until all are browned.

Carefully pour out the remaining grease in the skillet and wipe clean. Place the skillet back on the stove and add in @unsalted butter{1%tablespoon}.

Add in @shallot{1, finely chopped} and sauté until tender, ~{2-3%minutes}. Toss in @garlic{3%cloves, minced} and cook until fragrant, ~{1%minute}.

Stir in @green bell pepper{1%small, thinly sliced} and @red bell pepper{1%small, thinly sliced}. Continue cooking until the peppers soften, ~{2-3%minutes}.

Sprinkle in @Jamaican curry powder{3%teaspoons} and stir to toast the spice until fragrant, ~{1%minute}.

Pour in @full-fat coconut milk{1%14 oz can} and stir to combine. Allow the sauce to come to a boil for ~{1%minute}, then reduce the heat to the lowest setting.

Add all the meatballs into the sauce in a single layer. Spoon some of the sauce over each meatball.

Cover the skillet with a #lid{} and let the meatballs and sauce simmer together ~{20-25%minutes}. The internal temperature for pork doneness is right at 160°F.

Serve the jerk meatballs with coconut curry sauce immediately with @rice{for serving} and garnish with @sliced scallions{if desired}. Enjoy!
